Package: hd-dashboard
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3, systemd, hd-config
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian dashboard
 Shows the state of every hyprdebian system on one page. Each system POSTs a
 status report over HTTP every 15 minutes; the dashboard keeps the latest
 report of every system and a history of the load, the memory and the fullest
 pool, and judges each system on its last report: failed units, full or
 unhealthy pools, degraded arrays, failed timers, pending reboots and missing
 upgrades.
 .
 hd-dashboard.service runs it on port 80, as a user that systemd makes up,
 with the database in /var/lib/hd-dashboard. The settings are the key
 hd-dashboard in /etc/hyprdebian/config.json. Installing the package starts
 the service; opening its port in the firewall is left to the admin.
